When you polymorph into a monster, you usually cannot wield two weapons
at once. However, there are a handful of monster types who are allowed
to two-weapon; for instance, elf-lord, balrog, marilith, aleax. These
are the monsters which naturally have two "weapon" attacks: as a
monster, they hit twice with their wielded weapon.

I found out that the effect is cumulative ! Which means that if the player
polymorphs into such a monster _and_ wields two weapons, then he will be
able to land _four_ blows per turn.

I have tried with a Valkyrie, dual-wielding a blessed +7 Graywandir and
a blessed +7 silver spear, and polymorphed into an aleax ("permanent"
polymorph, with an amulet of unchanging). Gehenom and end-game were too
easy. Orcus was slained in one turn ! (the silver damage alone was
4d20). Is that intentional, or a bug ?


